Prompt Name
[Content Creator Starter]

Purpose
[The purpose is to help out starting content creators reach their goals effectively.]

Your Prompt
I am starting a YouTube channel targeting [TARGET_AUDIENCE]. What types of videos should I start posting on the channel to gain [SUBSCRIBER_GOAL] subscribers in [TIME_FRAME_GOAL]?

Design Justification
1. Did you use a specific framework? If yes, which one and why is it appropriate for this use case?
[The framework I used was RTF, because it was the best framework to use for this prompt. This was appropriate because it was the simplest and it was what I needed.]

2. Why did you structure your prompt this way? What specific elements did you include?
[I included a target audience because there are a lot of different consumers who have different interests on the platform and you can’t pinpoint one's person based on somebody else's interest.]

3. How does your prompt guide the AI effectively?
[My prompt is clear and reusable because it is vague enough that there is a clear goal but also specific enough that it can be changed based on what you want from the AI.]

4. What constraints or requirements did you add and why?
[I noticed that I had to ask specifically for examples or it would generate examples that I didn’t ask for. I noticed that prompts don’t need to be short but straight to the point in order to get the desired output

Refinement (if needed)
No refinement needed - scored 85+ on first attempt.
Final Reflection
[I learned that keeping the prompt short but direct helps guide the AI better than making the prompt over complicated. If you over complicate the prompt AI tries to supplement information that you don’t want.]

Best Used For
